	"h6StrongholdCyclops": {
		"name": {
			"singular": "Cyclops",
			"plural": "Cyclopes"
		},
		"description": "Cyclopes are the opposite of goblins. They too are \"failures\" of the orc experiments, but the cause lies in the blood of greater demons. The demonic half of their blood became dominant, and they turned into misshapen giants, twisted in body and mind by chaotic urges. Cyclopes usually stand over ten feet tall and look far more demon than human. One curious trait they all share is that they have only one eye: a huge, pupilless eye that glows red. No one knows where this mutation comes from; a theory widely accepted among wizards holds that it comes from the \"Sign of Chaos\", the ring-shaped serpent devouring itself, emblem of the Dragon God Urgash. Although they are peaceful by nature and as simple-minded as children, when they are hurt (in body or in spirit) they fall into an explosive, terrifying rage. This makes them a danger to everyone, their own kind included. Although many novels love tales of harnessing their power, in truth only the orcs have the strength, patience and courage to \"tame\" them, and to give them their rightful place in the villages as \"laborers\", and on the battlefield as heavy shock troops and \"siege weapons\".",
